    desc: "Abakuá (Ñáñigo), the secret Cross River (Ekpe/Efik) male-society drumming with the ekón bell and bonkó drums; its triplet-tinged 4/4 feel is a deep root of rumba columbia. [https://pulsewave.com/glossary-of-rhythms/]",
