    desc: "The Bahamian folk groove driven by a carpenter's saw scraped with a screwdriver, a goombay drum and accordion, accompanying the quadrille and heel-toe polka. The rural Family-Islands dance rhythm. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music_of_the_Bahamas ; https://islandhopperguides.com/bahamas/bahamian-culture/rake-and-scrape-rhythms-the-story-behind-the-bahamas-unique-musical-sound/]",
