    desc: "Sankirna jati Eka Tala (single 9-akshara laghu) played in misra-derived gati, 9 aksharas subdivided to 27 pulses, illustrating gati multiplication on an Eka cycle with finger-count accents. [https://www.academia.edu/7760865/Exploring_Nadai_The_concept_of_beat_subdivision_in_South_Indian_music]",
