    desc: "The chico defines the tatum, a rapid continuous pulse, but tellingly does not articulate the pulse falling on the beat — its strongest accent lands on the second tatum of each beat, giving candombe its forward lean. [Rocamora PhD thesis, Universidad de la República (iie.fing.edu.uy/~rocamora/phdthesis/candombe.html)] A steady eighth-note hi-hat keeps the time.",
