    desc: "Changüí from Guantánamo, ancestor of son, built on interlocking marímbula bass and bongó-del-monte; its syncopated swing predates fixed clave. Here the bongó/guayo accents sit in snareAccent and marímbula in bass. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Changui] A sparse quarter-note hi-hat opens the groove up.",
