    desc: "Nengón, the rural eastern Cuban proto-son from which changüí descends, with a simple call-and-response tres ostinato over marímbula bass. One of the oldest documented Cuban son roots. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Changui] A sparse quarter-note hi-hat opens the groove up.",
