    desc: "Kiribá, a Baracoa-region relative of nengón and changüí, an archaic eastern son form with cyclic tres and marímbula interplay. Part of the changüí complex of Guantánamo. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Changui] A sparse quarter-note hi-hat opens the groove up.",
