    desc: "Yuka, a secular Congo dance and drumming from Pinar del Río using three wooden yuka drums (caja, mula, cachimbo) with a guagua/reja bell, ancestor of the makuta and rumba. [https://cubamusicweek.org/databases/instruments/] A sparse quarter-note hi-hat opens the groove up.",
