    desc: "Chachalokafún (chachalokuá), a fundamental 4/4 batá toque associated with Obatalá and used widely across the liturgy; the okónkolo holds a steady timeline while iyá and itótele converse. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bat%C3%A1_drum] A sparse quarter-note hi-hat opens the groove up.",
