    desc: "Aluyá, a fast, fiery 6/8 batá toque for Changó, oricha of thunder, fire and drumming; its driving triple pulse accompanies the most energetic Changó dances. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bat%C3%A1_drum] A sparse quarter-note hi-hat opens the groove up.",
