    desc: "A batá toque for Babalú-Ayé (San Lázaro), oricha of disease and healing; a measured, limping 4/4 feel reflecting the orisha who walks with crutches. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bat%C3%A1_drum] A sparse quarter-note hi-hat opens the groove up.",
