    desc: "Martillo ('hammer'), the steady bongó pattern of son and salsa, marking continuous eighths with an accented open tone (macho) on beat 4. The bongocero's foundational groove. [https://rhythmnotes.net/salsa-rhythms/] A sparse quarter-note hi-hat opens the groove up.",
