    desc: "A sensual, swaying binary rhythm of the Kongo nation lwa, favouring 4/4 over the compound Rada meters, with hip-rolling syncopation. Among the few Vodou rhythms played duple rather than in 12/8. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haitian_Vodou_drumming ; https://en-academic.com/dic.nsf/enwiki/7930526] A sparse quarter-note hi-hat opens the groove up.",
