    desc: "The most common bomba seis, built on a 3+3+2 tresillo with a steady buleador while the subidor converses with the dancer's piquetes. The signature Afro-Puerto Rican barrel-drum groove. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bomba_(Puerto_Rico) ; http://www.alexpertout.com/lbomba.htm] A sparse quarter-note hi-hat opens the groove up.",
