    desc: "The principal compound-meter (6/8) bomba seis, played at a moderately fast tempo whose ternary feel challenges dancers and drummers alike. The deepest, most African-leaning of the bomba family. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bomba_(Puerto_Rico) ; https://folkways.si.edu/puerto-rican-bomba-plena-shared-traditions-distinct-rhythms/latin-world/music/article/smithsonian] A sparse quarter-note hi-hat opens the groove up.",
