    desc: "The hybrid sacred-secular song-form sung to the Virgin in Dominican folk-Catholic vigils, its Africanized variants driven by panderos and balsié in compound time. The most ubiquitous Dominican religious rhythm. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music_of_the_Dominican_Republic] A sparse quarter-note hi-hat opens the groove up.",
