    desc: "Jamaica's rural acoustic precursor to ska, with banjo, rhumba box and a relaxed afterbeat lilt that emphasizes the final beat of the bar. The folk root from which all later Jamaican pop grew. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ska ; https://routledgetextbooks.com/textbooks/9781138684478/globe/globe114.php] A sparse quarter-note hi-hat opens the groove up.",
