    desc: "The Rastafari hand-drumming heartbeat in 4/4: the thunder bass open on beat 1 and damped on beat 3, the funde holding the offbeat one-two, the repeater improvising. The sacred ancestor of reggae's one-drop. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nyabinghi_rhythm ; https://blog.zzounds.com/2018/04/27/foundational-beats-reggae-drums/] A sparse quarter-note hi-hat opens the groove up.",
