    desc: "The driving Sly-Dunbar 1970s rockers feel, adding a kick on beat 1 to the one-drop for a more insistent, four-square push. A heavier alternative to the one-drop. [https://blog.zzounds.com/2018/04/27/foundational-beats-reggae-drums/ ; https://rhythmnotes.net/reggae-drum-beats/] A sparse quarter-note hi-hat opens the groove up.",
