    genre: "Morenada", length: 8,
    voices: { bass: [0, 2, 4, 6], snareAccent: [0, 4], snareGhost: [3, 7], hatClosed: [0, 4], hhFoot: [0, 4] },
    desc: "The stately, heavy-stepping Afro-Andean dance of Oruro carnival; brass and the deep wankara/bombo dictate a slow, dragging duple march evoking enslaved Africans' chained gait. [Wikipedia 'Music of Bolivia'; remote-expeditions.com 'Music a Dances in Bolivia'] A sparse quarter-note hi-hat opens the groove up.",
