    desc: "The urban 'cueca brava' of Santiago's working-class quarters, sung by cuequeros over piano, guitar and panderos, keeping the 6/8-versus-3/4 sesquiáltera at brisk tempo. [marcachile.cl 'Types of Cueca'; Wikipedia 'Cueca'] A sparse quarter-note hi-hat opens the groove up.",
