    voices: { bass: [0, 6, 11], snareAccent: [8], hatClosed: [0, 4, 8, 12] },
    desc: "Original Chicago drill: dark halftime feel with the snare landing on beat 3, sparse booming 808s and triplet hat rolls. Ominous, slow-burning and heavy. [https://www.musicradar.com/how-to/how-to-program-6-classic-hip-hop-trap-and-grime-beats] A sparse quarter-note hi-hat opens the groove up.",
