    desc: "The stately, heavy-stepping Afro-Andean dance of Oruro carnival; brass and the deep wankara/bombo dictate a slow, dragging duple march evoking enslaved Africans' chained gait. [Wikipedia 'Music of Bolivia'; remote-expeditions.com 'Music a Dances in Bolivia'] The hi-hat barks open on the upbeats.",
