    desc: "A faster, more festive variant of the polka paraguaya played by galoperas; the binary-ternary overlap intensifies into a driving 6/8-against-3/4 gallop. [Wikipedia 'Paraguayan polka'; musicaparaguaya.jimdofree.com 'Types of folk music'] The hi-hat barks open on the upbeats.",
